msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5895
msgid ""
"Maximum equivalent hole diameter to compensate. For non-circular openings, the diameter of a "
"circle with the same sliced area is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5902
msgid "Counterbore bridge direction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5904
msgid ""
"Selects the line direction for the first counterbore bridge layer. Shortest Maximum minimizes the "
"longest bridge line. Shortest Minimum minimizes the shortest bridge line. Shortest Average "
"minimizes the average bridge-line length. Most Even minimizes the variation between bridge-line "
"lengths. Bridge Angle uses the Bridging angle setting; when that setting is automatic (0), "
"Shortest Maximum is used. Only directions with fully anchored lines are considered."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5906
msgid "Shortest Maximum"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5907
msgid "Shortest Minimum"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5908
msgid "Shortest Average"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5909
msgid "Most Even"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5910
msgid "Bridge Angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5916
msgid "Counterbore bridge anchor depth"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5918
msgid ""
"Extends each first counterbore bridge line only into the lower layer's actual perimeter paths "
"directly adjoining that counterbore. 0% keeps the bridge at the opening edge. For values below "
"100%, the locally outermost lower perimeter is left free; the requested depth is rounded to the "
"nearest remaining perimeter, with at least one perimeter reached when two or more are available. "
"100% may reach every safely available perimeter. A single lower perimeter always keeps edge-only "
"behavior. Outer walls and separate wall groups are not used as anchors. If no more than one third "
"of the bridge lines can reach their requested depth at both ends, the opening is left "
"uncompensated."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5926
msgid "Counterbore compensation layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5928
msgid ""
"Number of object layers to close, including the first bridge layer. Tracking stops early if the "
"opening no longer has a unique continuation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5936
